+
+Validation is structural: types, ranges, uniqueness, required fields, and catalog resolution. It does not judge scientific content, such as whether a species identification or a cover estimate is plausible.
+
+| Field | Required | Constraint |
+|---|---|---|
+| `visit_id` | yes | UUID, globally unique, never reused |
+| `base_revision_id` | no | Revision of the same visit that is either current or closed; omitted when the visit is first submitted or when the worker has no stated starting point. A base that names a candidate, another visit, or a revision the server does not hold is rejected under the concurrency rules, not by field validation. |
+| `payload.plot_id` | yes | UUID that resolves in the site catalog |
+| `payload.observed_on` | yes | Calendar date |
+| `payload.observers` | yes | List of observer names; each non-empty; no duplicates within the list |
+| `payload.species` | yes | List of species entries; each entry has a non-empty name, unique within the visit, and a numeric cover estimate between 0 and 100 |
+| `payload.notes` | yes | Free text; may be empty |
+| `idempotency_key` | yes | Client-minted key, unique per author, never reused for a different intended edit |
+
